---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
    <p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent tracking-[0.35em] uppercase mb-3">[ Dossier ]</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl mb-6">About WEAPON</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-fg-muted">
      <p class="text-lg">
        WEAPON is a reverse engineering field manual disguised as an interactive website. It teaches practical
        binary investigation methodology — not just terminology.
      </p>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mb-2">01</p>
        <h2 class="text-xl text-fg mb-2">The Philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          Most resources teach tools. WEAPON teaches investigation. You won't just learn "a CALL instruction calls
          a function" — you'll learn how to determine what function an unknown CALL invokes, what arguments it
          receives, and why that function matters.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Every lesson follows the same loop: <strong class="text-accent">Concept → Observation → Reasoning → Investigation</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mb-2">02</p>
        <h2 class="text-xl text-fg mb-2">Static & Educational</h2>
        <p>
          WEAPON is a fully static website. There is no backend, no database, and no authentication. All
          interactivity — visualizers, the instruction playground, and labs — runs entirely in your browser.
          Your progress is stored locally.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mb-2">03</p>
        <h2 class="text-xl text-fg mb-2">A Note on Ethics</h2>
        <p>
          Reverse engineering is a legitimate discipline used for malware analysis, vulnerability research,
          interoperability, and defensive security. WEAPON is designed for educational and defensive purposes only.
          The techniques described here should be applied only to software you own or are authorized to analyze.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="font-mono text-sm cursor-blink">WEAPON v0.1.0 — built with Astro, deployed on GitHub Pages.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>
